there's no avoiding death in me Oh even  if you're gifted enough to stay alive  corpses litter as many moonlit war-torn  locales it's a dark vision of Japan  during the aftermath of the violence and  Goku period in the early 17th century  it's a time of upheaval seeing through  new perspectives in neo by the fluid yet  demanding action game designs of team  ninja and from the narrative view of  navigator and trader William Adams as is  koa tech most traditional historical  figures Adams is reputation and prowess  as the first Western samurai are  elevated to supernatural status while  his skills and powers befitting a game  dense with hostiles and hazards it has  less in common with ninja gaiden and  more with the recent works of from  software  even when neo plays like a superb  spinoff of Dark Souls it has so far  shown potential in carving its own  identity  for instance while it shrines functions  similarly to Dark Souls is progress  saving bonfires they are not necessarily  safe havens since a shrine becomes  inaccessible if an enemy is nearby  by and large Neos demons and possessed  humans move with more assertiveness and  emotion than anyone you'll find in Dark  Souls you'll hear it in there growls  when they spot you  and in there grunts as they labor to  swing heavier weapons with two hands and  no matter how victorious you are winds  mean little unless you make it back to  your shrine to redeem your experience  and level up neo's environments can be  deceptive and you quickly learn to stay  on your toes at all times  demons stand in plain sight at the end  of hallways hoping you'll charge ahead  carelessly without anticipating his  buddy hiding around the corner you feel  smart when you've methodically lured a  possessed ninja into a one-on-one battle  conversely you feel idiotic when an  enemy capitalizes on your cockiness or  carelessness  that's the twisted beauty of neo it  pulverizes you the moment you don't  respect the foes abilities that includes  any attempts at brute forcing your way  to victory in neo even a weapon with  high attack power like an axe is better  in the hands of a patient player than a  persistently aggressive one aggressive  habits are understandable if you prefer  blood board since health replenishes  every time you deal damage conversely  stamina which determines the amount of  actions you can perform in the brief  span of time takes immense skill to  replenish a neo like the efficient  movements of a veteran samurai stamina  management in neo requires mindful  execution where every strike has purpose  the fact that enemies are also subject  to the limits of stamina is a standout  feature creating a level of combat death  not found in From Software's games  mastering stamina replenishment has as  of yet not been a prec juez it for  advancing a neo  instead you can defeat its bosses by  mixing thoughtful tactics and proactive  using of the games of many consumables  it's also an immense help that each  weapon has an expansive moveset spread  evenly across three fighting stances  it's gratifying to have the presence of  mind to switch between these poses in a  duel and besting an enemy without  wasting a single action makes you feel  like a veritable badass the myriad  variables to consider when it comes to  weapon choice combat stance and moment  to moment strategies almost feels  overwhelming but having all these  options is turning out to be one of neo  strengths the wealth of loot collected  from a dozen vanquished foes  can turn you into a weapons user of  multiple disciplines jumping from sword  to spear to hammer in the span of an  hour and even if you do become familiar  with all five weapon types there's also  the consideration of forgoing the  defensive security of an armored samurai  in favor of the less protected get more  agile ninja persona it remains to be  seen if this degree of diversity will be  a detriment to long-term success but so  far neo has been a punishing yet  gratifying excursion for Jack's of all  trades even after spending roughly 40  hours Neos progress menus implied I  still have another 40 to go given it's  collectibles have practical value I have  additional incentives to fully explore  the game's many already engrossing  environments the increased levels that  result from these thorough searches also  help make the boss fights less of a  headache given the varying degrees of  hardships I've encountered up to this  point I can't wait to see what devious  tricks the remaining bosses have up  their sleeves as I Forge through the  rest of the game  [Music]
 

